# UI/UX Pro Max (mandatory on UI turns)

This repo **always** uses UI/UX Pro Max for interface work. Follow `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md` whenever the task touches how something looks, feels, moves, or is interacted with. Do not skip it.

Source: [nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill](https://github.com/nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill)  
Installed via: `npx ui-ux-pro-max-cli init --ai cursor` (v2.x)

## Non-negotiable

**Search before inventing UI guidance.** Run the local search script, then apply results. Do not invent palettes, type scales, or UX rules from memory when the database has a match.

## Required when the task is visual / UX

1. Read `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md` and follow its workflow (analyze → search → apply).
2. Prefer project paths:
   - `python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<query>" --domain <domain>`
   - `--design-system` for new pages / system-wide direction
   - `--stack html-tailwind` (or detected stack) for implementation details
3. Priority order from the skill: Accessibility → Touch → Performance → Style → Layout → Typography/Color → Animation → Forms → Navigation → Charts.
4. Respect **existing** app chrome and user design rules for this Electron app; use Pro Max to improve clarity, a11y, spacing, and consistency — not to restyle the whole product unprompted.
5. Skip for pure backend / non-visual scripts unless the change affects UI.

## Never cut

Contrast, focus rings, keyboard access, tap targets (≥44px where interactive), labels on icon-only controls, reduced-motion respect, and anything the user explicitly asked for.

## Wiring (do not remove)

| Piece | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Skill (read/follow) | `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md` |
| Search CLI | `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py` |
| Always-on rule | `.cursor/rules/ui-ux-pro-max.mdc` |

Works with ponytail (small diffs), graphify (navigate first), and loop engineering (gate still proves done).
